+# FBI investigation and interview release copies of the Olson FD-302
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06. The official FBI Vault **9/11 Investigation 2001 09(Sep)** item supplied a 50-page PDF containing the September 11 interview and continuation. A prior attempt logged HTTP 403 for this item. The present direct request returned HTTP 200, a PDF signature and 2,068,660 bytes. Request conditions and access times differ. Both observations remain in the record. [FBI Vault release index, September investigation item](https://vault.fbi.gov/9-11%20Commission%20Report) · [Source pins](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Copy and filing fields
+
+| Observation | September investigation PDF | September interviews, part 05 viewer |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Form and location | FD-302 and FD-302a, physical pp. **9–10** | FD-302 and FD-302a, viewer pp. **11–12** |
+| Transcription date, selected header image | **09/11/2001** | **09/11/2001** |
+| Continuation's internal case field, selected image | **265D-NY-280350-302** | **265D-NY-280350-302** |
+| First report page, lower left handwritten notation | **`DR#174`** | **`DR#15`** |
+
+The investigation copy's first report page bears an upper-right review stamp dated **10-31-2012**. The prior viewer review reported a **2006** release marking and preserved an OCR year **2002** for the transcription-date field beside its visual **2001** reading. This pass checked the paired date and case fields on the images, both lower-left notations and the new stamp crop. It did not independently redate the earlier viewer release mark. The mark dates and face transcription fields describe separate events. [Earlier viewer and production review](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b993de9bfaf3ad0f24227ff3baae8b129c2cd1c2/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-box33-olson-production-images-2026-11-06/README.md)
+
+The previously identified Commission working-file entry **M-INT-00003811 / 265A-NY-280350-302-30777** is a separate production label. Retain its **265A** alongside the forms' **265D** and both handwritten **DR** values. The number marks provide exact retrieval keys. The issuing offices, request instruments and enclosure inventories are needed to determine what each mark means. Neither mark establishes that this document was produced under Request 14. [Commission file-unit locator](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2606244) · [Prior working-file crosswalk](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b993de9bfaf3ad0f24227ff3baae8b129c2cd1c2/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-box33-olson-production-images-2026-11-06/README.md)
+
+## Reported calls and scope of the match
+
+Both copies preserve the account that the first incoming conversation lasted **about one minute**. Both separately describe use of a direct line after that first call and contact with the Command Center. The continuation records that a subsequent conversation was cut off and that the interviewee did not know which kind of phone was used. The copy comparison preserves the office sequence and source uncertainty. It supplies neither a native call-event duration nor an operator, device, circuit or office-leg identifier. The two scans are reproductions of the same underlying interview account. [Prior interview context](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/b993de9bfaf3ad0f24227ff3baae8b129c2cd1c2/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-box33-olson-production-images-2026-11-06/README.md)
+
+I verified SHA-256 values for the acquired PDF and both held GIF responses. All 50 PDF pages were screened for embedded text and the file for standard embedded attachments. Both checks returned zero. The opening nine pages received bounded OCR locator screening. Substantive comparison covered the two target report pages and the paired viewer images. Seven selected OCR anchors matched in both representations. The first OCR comparison read **Conmand** at the held viewer anchor and stopped. Using the page segmentation mode recorded in the source pins found **Command**. Both OCR observations remain recorded. The anchor test does not establish full text or pixel equality, complete investigation-file contents or the historical accuracy of the interview.
+
+The public source pin uses the FBI collection index and exact item label. The original PDF bytes and the item response URL are retained in the native acquisition receipt. The public derivative excludes raw pages and direct links to unmasked contact fields.
+
+## Next discriminating records
+
+- **TEL02.** Seek the file or request register and enclosure manifest keyed to **DR#174** and **DR#15**, the Commission entry's release crosswalk, and the full part 05 PDF. The 50-page investigation PDF and the earlier 26-page viewer are distinct release objects. The interview notes or recording remain open.
+- **TEL03–TEL04.** Seek carrier/OSPS records, the office receiving and transfer legs, and the actual Command Center log. The precise caller/device/event associations and interpretation of the zero-duration exhibit remain open. The **DR** fields concern the document trail, separate from the telephone-event chain. [Telephone exhibit foundation](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/3011ef08a684fb9eda16d21cec92474c5bf162d4/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-court-foundation-and-docket-2026-11-09/README.md)
